**Answer: Soul Shards.**

In Classic WoW, summoning a Succubus requires a **Soul Shard**, and if she dies, you need another Shard to resummon her. Voidwalkers have the same cost, but the key difference is survivability:

- **Voidwalkers rarely die** — they're tanky, hold aggro with Torment/Suffering, and can heal themselves out of combat with Consume Shadows. One Shard can last an entire play session.
- **Succubus die constantly** — she's fragile, has no taunt (Soothing Kiss actually *reduces* threat), and mobs will frequently kill her, burning through your Shard supply.

Since Soul Shards require draining dying enemies (slowing down your grinding), most Warlocks stick with the Voidwalker as the economical, low-maintenance choice — even though the Succubus deals more damage. [end of text]


